    "content": {
      "rendered": "<div id=\"fh-jobpost\">\n<div style=\"background:#E4F3EA;border-left:5px solid #1E8E4E;border-radius:10px;padding:16px 18px;margin:0 0 22px;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#123D28;\"><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Amazon SDE 1 2026 is Amazon&rsquo;s university hiring opening for Software Dev Engineer I (Job ID 10454438) under ADCI &ndash; Karnataka, with locations listed as Bengaluru, Hyderabad and Chennai. It is open only to candidates who graduated in 2026 with a Bachelor&rsquo;s or higher degree in computer science, computer engineering or a related field. Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis, and no closing date is published.</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #E3E8E5;border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden;margin:0 0 24px;\">\n<div style=\"background:#0F3D2A;color:#fff;font-weight:800;font-size:17px;padding:13px 18px;\">Amazon SDE 1 2026 &mdash; job details at a glance</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;\">\n<div style=\"flex:1 1 260px;border-top:1px solid #EDF1EF;padding:12px 18px;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6C7B74;font-weight:700;\">Company</div>\n<div style=\"font-size:16.5px;color:#18241E;font-weight:600;margin-top:3px;\">Amazon (ADCI &ndash; Karnataka)</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1 1 260px;border-top:1px solid #EDF1EF;padding:12px 18px;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6C7B74;font-weight:700;\">Role</div>\n<div style=\"font-size:16.5px;color:#18241E;font-weight:600;margin-top:3px;\">Software Dev Engineer I, University Talent Acquisition</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1 1 260px;border-top:1px solid #EDF1EF;padding:12px 18px;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6C7B74;font-weight:700;\">Job ID</div>\n<div style=\"font-size:16.5px;color:#18241E;font-weight:600;margin-top:3px;\">10454438</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1 1 260px;border-top:1px solid #EDF1EF;padding:12px 18px;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6C7B74;font-weight:700;\">Locations</div>\n<div style=\"font-size:16.5px;color:#18241E;font-weight:600;margin-top:3px;\">Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Chennai</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1 1 260px;border-top:1px solid #EDF1EF;padding:12px 18px;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6C7B74;font-weight:700;\">Batch</div>\n<div style=\"font-size:16.5px;color:#18241E;font-weight:600;margin-top:3px;\">2026 graduates only</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1 1 260px;border-top:1px solid #EDF1EF;padding:12px 18px;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6C7B74;font-weight:700;\">Qualification</div>\n<div style=\"font-size:16.5px;color:#18241E;font-weight:600;margin-top:3px;\">Bachelor&rsquo;s or above in CS, CE or a related field</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1 1 260px;border-top:1px solid #EDF1EF;padding:12px 18px;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6C7B74;font-weight:700;\">Experience</div>\n<div style=\"font-size:16.5px;color:#18241E;font-weight:600;margin-top:3px;\">Fresher (internships preferred, not required)</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1 1 260px;border-top:1px solid #EDF1EF;padding:12px 18px;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6C7B74;font-weight:700;\">Salary</div>\n<div style=\"font-size:16.5px;color:#18241E;font-weight:600;margin-top:3px;\">Official: Not disclosed | Reported: &#8377;18&ndash;30 LPA (AmbitionBox, levels.fyi)</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1 1 260px;border-top:1px solid #EDF1EF;padding:12px 18px;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6C7B74;font-weight:700;\">Selection process</div>\n<div style=\"font-size:16.5px;color:#18241E;font-weight:600;margin-top:3px;\">Not published</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1 1 260px;border-top:1px solid #EDF1EF;padding:12px 18px;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6C7B74;font-weight:700;\">Deadline</div>\n<div style=\"font-size:16.5px;color:#18241E;font-weight:600;margin-top:3px;\">Rolling review, no closing date stated</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"ez-toc-container\" class=\"ez-toc-v2_0_90 counter-hierarchy ez-toc-counter ez-toc-light-blue ez-toc-container-direction\">\n<div class=\"ez-toc-title-container\"><p class=\"ez-toc-title\" style=\"cursor:inherit\">Job Summary</p>\n</div><nav><ul class='ez-toc-list ez-toc-list-level-1 ' ><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-1\" href=\"https://freshershunt.in/amazon-sde-1-2026/#Amazon_SDE_1_2026_%E2%80%93_full_job_details\" >Amazon SDE 1 2026 &ndash; full job details</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-2\" href=\"https://freshershunt.in/amazon-sde-1-2026/#What_you_will_do_in_the_Amazon_SDE_1_2026_role\" >What you will do in the Amazon SDE 1 2026 role</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-3\" href=\"https://freshershunt.in/amazon-sde-1-2026/#Amazon_SDE_1_2026_eligibility\" >Amazon SDE 1 2026 eligibility</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-4\" href=\"https://freshershunt.in/amazon-sde-1-2026/#Amazon_SDE_1_2026_selection_process\" >Amazon SDE 1 2026 selection process</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-5\" href=\"https://freshershunt.in/amazon-sde-1-2026/#Documents_required\" >Documents required</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-6\" href=\"https://freshershunt.in/amazon-sde-1-2026/#Preparation_tips_for_Amazon_SDE_1_2026_interviews\" >Preparation tips for Amazon SDE 1 2026 interviews</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-7\" href=\"https://freshershunt.in/amazon-sde-1-2026/#Expected_salary_for_Amazon_SDE_1_2026\" >Expected salary for Amazon SDE 1 2026</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-8\" href=\"https://freshershunt.in/amazon-sde-1-2026/#How_to_apply_for_Amazon_SDE_1_2026\" >How to apply for Amazon SDE 1 2026</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-9\" href=\"https://freshershunt.in/amazon-sde-1-2026/#About_Amazon\" >About Amazon</a></li><li class='ez-toc-page-1 ez-toc-heading-level-2'><a class=\"ez-toc-link ez-toc-heading-10\" href=\"https://freshershunt.in/amazon-sde-1-2026/#Frequently_asked_questions\" >Frequently asked questions</a></li></ul></nav></div>\n<h2 style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3;margin:26px 0 12px;color:#111;\"><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"Amazon_SDE_1_2026_%E2%80%93_full_job_details\"></span>Amazon SDE 1 2026 &ndash; full job details<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2>\n<p style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 14px;color:#24312B;\">The Amazon SDE 1 2026 opening is an entry-level software engineering position run by Amazon&rsquo;s University Talent Acquisition team. It is the first rung of the SDE ladder, so new hires write production code from day one.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 14px;color:#24312B;\">The posting sits under Amazon Development Centre India (ADCI) &ndash; Karnataka, while the job details list three cities: Bengaluru, Hyderabad and Chennai. Amazon reviews profiles as they arrive, so apply early.</p>\n<div style=\"background:#FDEBEA;border-left:5px solid #C8372B;border-radius:10px;padding:15px 18px;margin:0 0 20px;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#5B1A14;\"><strong>Hard filter:</strong> graduating in 2026 is a <em>basic</em> qualification, not a preference. If you are in the 2027 batch or graduated in 2025 or earlier, this Amazon SDE 1 2026 requisition is not for you. Students still studying should look at the internship list instead.</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"background:#FFF6E3;border-left:5px solid #E1A006;border-radius:10px;padding:15px 18px;margin:0 0 20px;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:#4A3706;\"><strong>Check before you apply:</strong> the job details panel tags this SDE opening under &ldquo;Administrative Support&rdquo;, which looks like an employer labelling error. The role text itself is clearly software development. Also, the posting does not say which of the three cities you will be placed in, so state your preference in the application and confirm it with the recruiter.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3;margin:26px 0 12px;color:#111;\"><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"What_you_will_do_in_the_Amazon_SDE_1_2026_role\"></span>What you will do in the Amazon SDE 1 2026 role<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2>\n<p style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 14px;color:#24312B;\">Amazon describes the work in broad terms. In plain language, the Amazon SDE 1 2026 team expects you to:</p>\n<ul style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:22px;color:#24312B;\">\n<li>Work with senior engineers from several disciplines to shape and ship new products and services</li>\n<li>Build software that runs on very large distributed computing systems</li>\n<li>Help run prediction workloads on distributed infrastructure at high speed and scale</li>\n<li>Create storage, indexing and query systems that stay reliable, scalable and cheap to run</li>\n<li>Turn loosely defined problems into a working design and then code it</li>\n<li>Deliver tested, high-quality code inside short agile cycles measured in weeks</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3;margin:26px 0 12px;color:#111;\"><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"Amazon_SDE_1_2026_eligibility\"></span>Amazon SDE 1 2026 eligibility<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2>\n<p style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 14px;color:#24312B;\">The two basic requirements for the Amazon SDE 1 2026 role are firm: a Bachelor&rsquo;s degree or higher in computer science, computer engineering or a closely related field, and a 2026 graduation year.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 14px;color:#24312B;\">Amazon also lists preferred qualifications. These strengthen a profile but are not cut-offs:</p>\n<ul style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:22px;color:#24312B;\">\n<li>One or more earlier technical internships</li>\n<li>Hands-on work with distributed or multi-tier systems, algorithms and relational databases</li>\n<li>Exposure to optimisation maths such as linear and nonlinear programming</li>\n<li>Clear explanation of technical problems and the fixes you chose</li>\n<li>Comfort with vague or open-ended problems and abstract thinking</li>\n</ul>\n<div style=\"background:#F3F6F4;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#43514A;\"><strong>Not stated by Amazon:</strong> minimum CGPA, backlog rules, bond, joining date and exact branch list. Treat any figure you see elsewhere for these as unconfirmed.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3;margin:26px 0 12px;color:#111;\"><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"Amazon_SDE_1_2026_selection_process\"></span>Amazon SDE 1 2026 selection process<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2>\n<p style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 14px;color:#24312B;\">Amazon has not published the Amazon SDE 1 2026 selection rounds. Based on how Amazon usually hires new-grad SDEs, plan for an online coding assessment, followed by two or three technical interviews on data structures, algorithms and basic system design, with Leadership Principles questions woven into each round. Use this as a preparation plan, not a guaranteed format.</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3;margin:26px 0 12px;color:#111;\"><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"Documents_required\"></span>Documents required<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2>\n<ul style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:22px;color:#24312B;\">\n<li>Updated one-page resume (build one free with our <a href=\"https://freshershunt.in/resume-builder/\">Resume Builder</a>)</li>\n<li>Degree certificate or provisional certificate showing 2026 graduation</li>\n<li>Semester mark sheets</li>\n<li>Government photo ID</li>\n<li>Internship letters or project links (GitHub, portfolio), if any</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3;margin:26px 0 12px;color:#111;\"><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"Preparation_tips_for_Amazon_SDE_1_2026_interviews\"></span>Preparation tips for Amazon SDE 1 2026 interviews<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2>\n<p style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 14px;color:#24312B;\">Most applicants lose marks in the coding round, so put most of your time there. Practise arrays, strings, trees, graphs, heaps and dynamic programming until medium problems feel routine, and always talk through time and space complexity.</p>\n<p style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 14px;color:#24312B;\">For Amazon SDE 1 2026 interviews, read Amazon&rsquo;s 16 Leadership Principles and prepare two short STAR stories for each of the common ones, such as Customer Obsession, Ownership and Dive Deep. For projects, be ready to explain trade-offs, not just features. Our free <a href=\"https://freshershunt.in/tools/\">career tools</a> and this guide to a <a href=\"https://freshershunt.in/self-introduction-for-interview/\">self introduction for interview</a> help with the opening minutes.</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3;margin:26px 0 12px;color:#111;\"><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"Expected_salary_for_Amazon_SDE_1_2026\"></span>Expected salary for Amazon SDE 1 2026<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2>\n<p style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 14px;color:#24312B;\">Amazon does not publish pay on this listing. Reported figures for Amazon SDE 1 freshers in India sit roughly between &#8377;18 LPA and &#8377;30 LPA. AmbitionBox data cited in 2026 puts the 0&ndash;1 year band at about &#8377;27&ndash;30 LPA, while levels.fyi shows an average SDE I package in Bengaluru near &#8377;26 LPA with base pay around &#8377;18 LPA. These are self-reported numbers, not an offer, so ask the recruiter for the written break-up of base, joining bonus and stock.</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3;margin:26px 0 12px;color:#111;\"><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"How_to_apply_for_Amazon_SDE_1_2026\"></span>How to apply for Amazon SDE 1 2026<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2>\n<ol style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 16px;padding-left:22px;color:#24312B;\">\n<li>Open the official Amazon Jobs page for Job ID 10454438: <a href=\"https://www.amazon.jobs/en/jobs/10454438/software-dev-engineer-i-amazon-university-talent-acquisition\" rel=\"nofollow sponsored noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Apply on amazon.jobs</a></li>\n<li>Sign in or create a candidate account on Amazon Jobs</li>\n<li>Upload your resume and fill in education details, including your 2026 graduation date</li>\n<li>Answer the screening questions honestly and pick your preferred city</li>\n<li>Submit and track the status in your candidate portal</li>\n</ol>\n<div style=\"background:#F3F6F4;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 20px;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#43514A;\">More openings: <a href=\"https://freshershunt.in/amazon-off-campus-drive-2027/\">Amazon Off Campus Drive 2027</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://freshershunt.in/amazon-internship-2027/\">Amazon Internship 2027</a> &middot; <a href=\"https://freshershunt.in/companies-hiring-freshers/\">Companies hiring freshers</a></p>\n</div>\n<h2 style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3;margin:26px 0 12px;color:#111;\"><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"About_Amazon\"></span>About Amazon<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2>\n<p style=\"font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.75;margin:0 0 14px;color:#24312B;\">Amazon is a global technology company spanning e-commerce, cloud computing through AWS, devices, streaming and advertising. Its India development centres in Bengaluru, Hyderabad and Chennai build software for teams worldwide, and the company is known for a demanding, customer-focused engineering culture.</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3;margin:26px 0 12px;color:#111;\"><span class=\"ez-toc-section\" id=\"Frequently_asked_questions\"></span>Frequently asked questions<span class=\"ez-toc-section-end\"></span></h2>\n<details style=\"border:1px solid #E3E8E5;border-radius:10px;padding:12px 16px;margin:0 0 10px;\">\n<summary style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:16.5px;color:#123D28;cursor:pointer;\">What is the salary for Amazon SDE 1 2026?</summary>\n<p style=\"margin:10px 0 2px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;color:#24312B;\">Amazon has not disclosed the salary on this listing. Reported figures for fresher SDE 1 roles in India range from about &#8377;18 LPA to &#8377;30 LPA (AmbitionBox, levels.fyi). Treat these as estimates and confirm the break-up with the recruiter.</p>\n</details>\n<details style=\"border:1px solid #E3E8E5;border-radius:10px;padding:12px 16px;margin:0 0 10px;\">\n<summary style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:16.5px;color:#123D28;cursor:pointer;\">Who is eligible for Amazon SDE 1 2026?</summary>\n<p style=\"margin:10px 0 2px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;color:#24312B;\">Candidates with a Bachelor&rsquo;s degree or higher in computer science, computer engineering or a related field who graduated in 2026. The 2026 graduation year is a basic qualification, so other batches do not qualify.</p>\n</details>\n<details style=\"border:1px solid #E3E8E5;border-radius:10px;padding:12px 16px;margin:0 0 10px;\">\n<summary style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:16.5px;color:#123D28;cursor:pointer;\">Is an internship required for this Amazon role?</summary>\n<p style=\"margin:10px 0 2px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;color:#24312B;\">No. Previous technical internships are listed as preferred, not mandatory. Strong coding skills, projects and knowledge of distributed systems, algorithms and databases also help your profile.</p>\n</details>\n<details style=\"border:1px solid #E3E8E5;border-radius:10px;padding:12px 16px;margin:0 0 10px;\">\n<summary style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:16.5px;color:#123D28;cursor:pointer;\">Where is the Amazon SDE 1 2026 job located?</summary>\n<p style=\"margin:10px 0 2px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;color:#24312B;\">The posting is under ADCI &ndash; Karnataka and lists Bengaluru, Hyderabad and Chennai. Your final city is not stated, so confirm it with the recruiter.</p>\n</details>\n<details style=\"border:1px solid #E3E8E5;border-radius:10px;padding:12px 16px;margin:0 0 10px;\">\n<summary style=\"font-weight:700;font-size:16.5px;color:#123D28;cursor:pointer;\">How do I apply for this Amazon SDE opening?</summary>\n<p style=\"margin:10px 0 2px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.75;color:#24312B;\">Apply on the official amazon.jobs page for Job ID 10454438. Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis with no closing date, so apply early. Amazon never charges any fee.</p>\n</details>\n<p><a id=\"fh-apply-src\" href=\"https://www.amazon.jobs/en/jobs/10454438/software-dev-engineer-i-amazon-university-talent-acquisition\" rel=\"nofollow sponsored noopener\" hidden target=\"_blank\">Apply on official portal</a></p>\n</div>\n<p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"JobPosting\",\"title\":\"Software Dev Engineer I, Amazon University Talent Acquisition\",\"description\":\"Entry-level Software Dev Engineer I role for 2026 graduates with a Bachelor's degree or above in computer science, computer engineering or a related field. Work on large-scale distributed systems, storage, indexing and query services in an agile team. Locations: Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Chennai.\",\"identifier\":{\"@type\":\"PropertyValue\",\"name\":\"Amazon\",\"value\":\"10454438\"},\"datePosted\":\"2026-09-29\",\"employmentType\":\"FULL_TIME\",\"hiringOrganization\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Amazon\",\"sameAs\":\"https://www.amazon.jobs\"},\"jobLocation\":[{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"address\":{\"@type\":\"PostalAddress\",\"addressLocality\":\"Bengaluru\",\"addressRegion\":\"KA\",\"addressCountry\":\"IN\"}},{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"address\":{\"@type\":\"PostalAddress\",\"addressLocality\":\"Hyderabad\",\"addressRegion\":\"TS\",\"addressCountry\":\"IN\"}},{\"@type\":\"Place\",\"address\":{\"@type\":\"PostalAddress\",\"addressLocality\":\"Chennai\",\"addressRegion\":\"TN\",\"addressCountry\":\"IN\"}}],\"educationRequirements\":{\"@type\":\"EducationalOccupationalCredential\",\"credentialCategory\":\"bachelor degree\"},\"experienceRequirements\":\"no requirements\",\"directApply\":false,\"url\":\"https://www.amazon.jobs/en/jobs/10454438/software-dev-engineer-i-amazon-university-talent-acquisition\"}</script><br />\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"NewsArticle\",\"headline\":\"Amazon SDE 1 2026: Software Dev Engineer I for 2026 Graduates\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-11-23\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-11-23\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Freshershunt\",\"url\":\"https://freshershunt.in\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Freshershunt\",\"url\":\"https://freshershunt.in\"},\"mainEntityOfPage\":\"https://freshershunt.in/amazon-sde-1-2026/\"}</script><br />\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is the salary for Amazon SDE 1 2026?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Amazon has not disclosed the salary on this listing. Reported figures for fresher SDE 1 roles in India range from about &#8377;18 LPA to &#8377;30 LPA (AmbitionBox, levels.fyi). Treat these as estimates and confirm the break-up with the recruiter.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Who is eligible for Amazon SDE 1 2026?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Candidates with a Bachelor&rsquo;s degree or higher in computer science, computer engineering or a related field who graduated in 2026. The 2026 graduation year is a basic qualification, so other batches do not qualify.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Is an internship required for this Amazon role?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"No. Previous technical internships are listed as preferred, not mandatory. Strong coding skills, projects and knowledge of distributed systems, algorithms and databases also help your profile.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Where is the Amazon SDE 1 2026 job located?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The posting is under ADCI &ndash; Karnataka and lists Bengaluru, Hyderabad and Chennai. Your final city is not stated, so confirm it with the recruiter.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How do I apply for this Amazon SDE opening?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Apply on the official amazon.jobs page for Job ID 10454438. Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis with no closing date, so apply early. Amazon never charges any fee.\"}}]}</script></p>\n<div style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px;\" class=\"sharethis-inline-share-buttons\" ></div>",
